# sa535m_emac0_rgmii_mac2mac_1000mbps

Switches EMAC0 on SA535M to RGMII MAC-to-MAC mode at 1000 Mbps: no PHY chip is
present, so the link is described with a `fixed-link` instead of an
MDIO-managed `phy-handle`.

## Platform
- SoC: SA535M (`msm-id = 703`)
- Board variants: EMMC TDP (`0x10030 0x0`), NAND TDP (`0x10030 0x20000`)

## EMAC0
- Interface: RGMII (`rgmii`, no internal delay) — on the echo-ethqos driver
  (`ethqos_configure_echo()`), the RGMII delay/DLL registers are hardcoded
  per speed and not gated by the DT `phy-mode` string, so `rgmii`/`rgmii-id`/
  `rgmii-rxid`/`rgmii-txid` are all functionally identical here.
- Link: fixed-link, 1000 Mbps full-duplex
- MDIO/phy-handle: removed (no PHY to manage)
